infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title OT vs CRDT: two routes to convergence
  desc Both make every replica end up identical; they pay for it in different places
  compares
    - label Operational transformation
      children
        - label Index-based operations
          desc Insert at 1, delete at 2. Positions are shifted against concurrent edits
        - label Central server defines the order
          desc Each op carries its base revision; the server transforms and assigns the next
        - label Compact, hard to verify
          desc Small messages, but transform functions for rich documents are bug-prone
    - label CRDT
      children
        - label Every element has a unique ID
          desc Insert X after ID a1. Deletes become tombstones instead of removals
        - label Operations commute
          desc Any delivery order converges, so offline and peer-to-peer sync just work
        - label Metadata and cleanup cost
          desc IDs and tombstones add overhead; garbage collection needs all replicas caught up
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
